{"id":"st292-1","designation":"ST 292-1","title":"Serial Digital Interface 1.5 Gb/s — 1.5 Gb/s Signal/Data Serial Interface","state":"stabilized","suite":"292","official":{"family_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/doc/st292-1/","latest_url":"https://pub.smpte.org/latest/st292-1/","checked_at":"2026-11-11"},"scope":"This standard defines a bit-serial data structure and the coaxial cable interface specifications for 1.5 Gb/s [nominal] Signal/Data Serial Interface to carry either 1280×720, 1920×1080 or 2048×1080 active pixel formats mapped into the 1.5 Gb/s payload. This standard defines the method of serializing the parallel source format data to a serial bit stream. This interface may also carry packetized data mapped into the 1.5 Gb/s transport payload providing the constraints imposed by the reference source image formats are observed. This standard specifies a coaxial cable interface suitable for application where the signal loss does not exceed an amount specified by the receiver manufacturer, typical loss amounts would be in the range of up to 20 dB at one-half the clock frequency.","outline":[{"level":1,"title":"1 Scope","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"2 Conformance Notation","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"3 Normative References","page":3},{"level":1,"title":"4 Source Format Data","page":4},{"level":2,"title":"4.1 For this interface, the source data shall be 10-bit words. The source data may be an uncompressed video source or packetized data constrained by the pixel array of the referenced source image formats.","page":4},{"level":1,"title":"5 Interface Data Format","page":5},{"level":1,"title":"5.1 Digital active line and digital line blanking shall consist of 10-bit words as defined by the source format document. Data values 000h to 003h and 3FCh to 3FFh shall be used exclusively for synchronization purposes.","page":5},{"level":1,"title":"6 Serial Data Format","page":6},{"level":1,"title":"7 Channel Coding","page":7},{"level":1,"title":"8 Coaxial Cable Interface","page":7},{"level":1,"title":"9 Payload Identifier","page":9},{"level":1,"title":"Annex A Channel Code (Informative)","page":15},{"level":1,"title":"Annex B Timing Reference Codes (Informative)","page":16},{"level":1,"title":"Annex C Source Signal Formats (Informative)","page":17},{"level":1,"title":"Annex D Audio Data Mapping (Informative)","page":19},{"level":1,"title":"Bibliography (Informative)","page":20}],"definitions":[],"keywords":[{"term":"Serial Digital Interface","zh":"串行数字接口","abbr":"SDI","category":"tv","source":"curated"},{"term":"Wide-Screen Scanning","zh":"宽银幕扫描","abbr":"","category":"film","source":"curated"},{"term":"Connector","zh":"连接器","abbr":"","category":"tv","source":"curated"},{"term":"Audio Polarity","zh":"音频极性","abbr":"","category":"audio","source":"curated"},{"term":"Test Pattern","zh":"测试图","abbr":"","category":"measurement","source":"curated"},{"term":"High Dynamic Range","zh":"高动态范围","abbr":"HDR","category":"hdr","source":"curated"},{"term":"Hybrid Log-Gamma","zh":"混合对数伽马","abbr":"HLG","category":"hdr","source":"curated"},{"term":"ITU-R BT.2100","zh":"BT.2100","abbr":"BT.2100","category":"hdr","source":"curated"},{"term":"Format Conversion","zh":"格式转换","abbr":"","category":"tv","source":"curated"},{"term":"Image Mapping","zh":"图像映射","abbr":"","category":"hdr","source":"curated"},{"term":"Perceptual Quantizer","zh":"感知量化","abbr":"PQ","category":"hdr","source":"curated"},{"term":"EAV","zh":"","abbr":"EAV","category":"other","source":"acronym"}],"refs":[{"id":"st291","designation":"ST 291"},{"id":"rp2077","designation":"RP 2077"},{"id":"st274","designation":"ST 274"},{"id":"st296","designation":"ST 296"},{"id":"st352","designation":"ST 352"},{"id":"st2048-2","designation":"ST 2048-2"},{"id":"rp184","designation":"RP 184"},{"id":"st2084","designation":"ST 2084"},{"id":"rp198","designation":"RP 198"},{"id":"st2048-1","designation":"ST 2048-1"},{"id":"rp291-2","designation":"RP 291-2"},{"id":"st259","designation":"ST 259"}],"cited_by":[{"id":"e